          %h2#PrincipalConnections
            %strong Principal connections
          %h3#model_layer Model Layer
          %h4#motivation Motivation
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
                implies that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
                is not just given by a closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
                but by a refinement of that to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            %li
              %p
                analogous arguments show that more generally a configuration of the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+field"} Yang-Mills field
                for some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is a
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            %li
              %p
                analogous arguments say that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                are given by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
          %p
            In this way all of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            is much the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            and all of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher gauge theory
            is much the study of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-connections"} principal infinity-connections
          %p
            More is true: also a configuration of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            is represented by a connection, in this case a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+group"} Poincare group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            satisfying an extra condition (that “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"}> solders
            ” it to the underlying manifold).
          %h4#DeligneCohomology Deligne cohomology
          %p
            It turns out that one of the many equivalent incarnations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SemanticsLayer"} Semantics layer
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne cohomology
            taken at face value.
          %h5#PreliminariesOnSheafCohomology Preliminaries on sheaf cohomology
          %p
            In order to be somewhat self-contained, this section reviews some elements of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            specified to the context that we need. It also sets up some notation. The definition of the Deligne complex itself is
            %a{:href => "#TheDeligneComplex"} below
            in def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheSmoothDeligneComplex"}
          %p
            Recall the following definition, which is discussed in much detail in the chapter
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} geometry of physics – smooth sets
          #Smooth0Types.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Write
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n_1} \to \mathbb{R}^{n_2}
                  between these;
              %li
                %p
                  whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
                  is given by “differentially
                  = succeed "\u201D," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
                  of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
                  to an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
