                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
                  if it is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
                  (of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
          #HomotopyFibersViaFactorizationLemma.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              For our purpose the main use of this structure is to compute
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
              via the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
            %ol
              %li
                %p every chain map may be replaced, up to weak equivalence of its domain, by a fibration;
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
                  of a chain map is the ordinary fiber of any of its fibration replacements.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              That the properties in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantOnjectStructureOnChSmooth"}
              are interpreted in sheaves simply means that they apply
              = succeed "-wise." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet \colon A_\bullet \to B_\bullet
              is a weak equivalence precisely if the underlying presheaf of chain complexes becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              for each point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in each Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              after restricting (via the presheaf structure maps) to a small enough
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              of that point. Similarly for epimorphisms.
          #HomotopyPullbacksPreservedbyInclusionIntoAllSmoothHomotopyTypes.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              There is a canonical map of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theories"} homotopy theories
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_+(Smooth0Type)
              to the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              which is given by applying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              followed by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+products"} homotopy fiber products
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal construction
              that already captures most of the relevant properties of the Deligne complex. In this way it is sufficient to concentrate on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_+(Smooth0Type)
              for much of the theory.
          %p
            When writing out the components of chain complexes we will use square brackets always denote the group in degree-0 to the far right, and the group in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            being
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            steps to the left from that.
          #DeloopingsOfAbelianSheaf.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ab(Smooth0Type) = Sh(CartSp,Ab)
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaf
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbf{B}^n A)_{\bullet}
                    \\coloneqq
                    A[-n]
                    \=
                    \\left[
                    A
                    
                    \\to 0 \to \cdots \to 0
                    \\right]
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              of sheaves concentrated on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #LogDiffInSmoothContext.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              There is a weak equivalence, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantOnjectStructureOnChSmooth"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ]
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left[\mathbb{Z}\to \mathbb{R} \right]
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    U(1)
            %p
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi mod
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \mathbb{R}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{mod\,\mathbb{Z}}}
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\to&amp; U(1)
                    }
            %p
              (which is just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+sequence"} exponential sequence
              regarded as a chain map).
            %p
              The de Rham differential
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extends
              through this equivalence to produce a morphism denoted
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi d
                      %mi log
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d} log
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo →
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi d
                                  %mi log
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{R}) &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^1
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}} &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\mathbf{d} log}}
                    \\\
                    U(1)
                    \\,.
                    }
            %p
              On a given
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "-reduction" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of that is the constant sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat U(1)
              of example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RepresentableSheavesAndTheirConstantVersion"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♭
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                        %mi log
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to
                    \\flat U(1) \hookrightarrow U(1)
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d} log}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^1
                    \\,.
          %p
            Under addition of differential forms, the sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Ω
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Omega}^k
            of example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheavesOfFormsAndDeRhamDifferential"}
            becomes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
          #DeRhamResolutionOfConstantFunctions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ♭
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ^
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{(\flat \mathbf{B}^{n+1}\mathbb{R})}_\bullet \in Ch(Smooth0Type)
              for the complex of sheaves given by the truncated
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ♭
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ^
                      %mo •
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi d
                      %msubsup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Ω
                        %mi cl
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat{(\flat \mathbf{B}^{n+1}\mathbb{R})}_\bullet
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left[
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^1
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^2
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\cdots
                    \\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^{n+1}_{cl}
                    \\right]
                    \\,.
          #TheDeRhamResolutionOfConstantFunctions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p The morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ♭
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo ♭
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ^
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\flat \mathbf{B}^{n+1}\mathbb{R})_\bullet
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\widehat{(\flat \mathbf{B}^{n+1}\mathbb{R})}_\bullet
            %p
              given by the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♭
                            %mi ℝ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\flat \mathbb{R}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    0
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    0
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\cdots
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    0
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \cdots
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^1
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^2
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}&amp;
                    \\cdots
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{d}}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^{n+1}_{cl}
                    }
            %p
              is a weak equivalence in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantOnjectStructureOnChSmooth"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+lemma"} Poincaré lemma
              %em is
              the Poincaré Lemma.
          %p
            Every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Type
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet \in Ch_+(Smooth0Type)
            serves as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            theory on smooth manifolds. Abelian sheaf cohomology has a general abstract characterization (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-spaces"} derived hom-spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
            \.
          #CechComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Čech complex)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet \in Ch_+(Smooth0Type)
              be a sheaf of chain complexes. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{i_0, \cdots, i_k}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to an
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %p
              The
              %strong Čech cochain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
