              the statement is immediate.
          %h5#TheChernCharacter The Chern character
          %p
            While the explicit definition of the Deligne complex in def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheSmoothDeligneComplex"}
            is easy enough, all its good abstract properties are best understood by realizing that it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            of a kind of higher abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            map with the closed differential forms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Omega}^{n+1}_{cl}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyFiberProductCharacterization"}
            below.
          #ChernCharacterMap.num_defn
            %h6#definition_13 Definition
            %p Write
