          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              The morphism in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChernCharacterMap"}
              is just the traditional map from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
              coefficients to that with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              coefficients given for instance via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
              simply by forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
              however it is useful to think of this map as the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            %p
              While this is easy enough to construct in itself, the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
              here is not a fibration in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FibrantOnjectStructureOnChSmooth"}
              (having as non-trivial component the inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of this map plays a crucial role in the theory, and so in view of remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyFibersViaFactorizationLemma"}
              we consider now a fibration
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              of this map
